@baseUrl=http://localhost:8000/api/v1/payouts
@payoutID=REPLACE_WITH_PAYOUT_ID
@poolId=REPLACE_WITH_POOL_ID
@supplierToken=REPLACE_WITH_SUPPLIER_ACCESS_TOKEN
@adminToken=REPLACE_WITH_ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN

# amount is looked up server-side from the pool's ProductOffer.price — not
# accepted from the client. The platform's margin is fixed by the admin up
# front (baked into Pool.pricePerUnit vs. that price when the pool is
# created), so it's never recomputed from actual retailer payments. A
# payout is auto-created the moment an admin PATCHes the pool's Delivery to
# DELIVERED (see DeliveryController.update()/SupplierPayoutController.listeners()) —
# Thawani has no vendor/marketplace payout capability, so this is purely an
# internal record an admin pays out manually, outside Thawani entirely.

### manual fallback: create a payout for a pool whose delivery is DELIVERED
### (ADMIN only) — normally unnecessary since marking the delivery DELIVERED
### auto-creates this; use it only if that auto-create was skipped (e.g. the
### pool's product offer couldn't be found at that moment)

POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
    "pool_ref": "{{poolId}}"
}

### list my own payouts (SUPPLIER — pools built from their own offers)

GET {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{supplierToken}}

### list every payout (ADMIN)

GET {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### get a payout by id (owning SUPPLIER, or ADMIN for any)

GET {{baseUrl}}/{{payoutID}}
Authorization: Bearer {{supplierToken}}

### record the manual transfer and mark it COMPLETED (ADMIN only) —
### paidAt is auto-stamped if not supplied

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/{{payoutID}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
    "status": "COMPLETED",
    "transactionReference": "bank-transfer-ref-123"
}
